    "ruleId": "frame-title",
    "platform": "custom",
    "slug": "frame-title",
    "title": "Add a title to embedded frames",
    "summary": "Every iframe, such as a video, map or chat widget, needs a title describing its content.",
    "reviewedAt": "2026-11-16T00:00:00Z",
    "wrong": "An `<iframe>` without a `title` is announced only as \"frame\", so people can't tell a video from a map or a payment form.",
    "affects": "Screen reader users moving between frames or landmarks on the page.",
    "howToFix": "Add a short, unique `title` to every `<iframe>` that says what's inside, such as \"Video: How to assemble the oak chair\" or \"Map of our showroom\". Third-party embed snippets often leave it out; add it yourself after pasting the snippet.",
    "codeSnippet": "### Incorrect\n```html\n<iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/abc123\"></iframe>\n```\n\n### Correct\n```html\n<iframe\n  src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/abc123\"\n  title=\"Video: How to assemble the oak chair\"\n  loading=\"lazy\"\n  allowfullscreen></iframe>\n```\n\n### React / Next.js (JSX)\n```jsx\n<iframe\n  src={`https://www.youtube.com/embed/${videoId}`}\n  title={`Video: ${videoTitle}`}\n  loading=\"lazy\"\n  allowFullScreen\n/>\n```\n\n### Vue\n```vue\n<template>\n  <iframe\n    :src=\"`https://www.youtube.com/embed/${videoId}`\"\n    :title=\"`Video: ${videoTitle}`\"\n    loading=\"lazy\"\n    allowfullscreen\n  />\n</template>\n```",
    "howToCheck": "In the browser's accessibility tree, check each iframe has a name. With a screen reader, move to the frame and confirm the title is announced. Then rescan with EveryVisitor.",
    "bodyMd": "# Add a title to embedded frames\n\n## What's wrong\n\nAn `<iframe>` without a `title` is announced only as \"frame\", so people can't tell a video from a map or a payment form.\n\n## Who it affects\n\nScreen reader users moving between frames or landmarks on the page.\n\n## How to fix on a custom-coded site\n\nAdd a short, unique `title` to every `<iframe>` that says what's inside, such as \"Video: How to assemble the oak chair\" or \"Map of our showroom\". Third-party embed snippets often leave it out; add it yourself after pasting the snippet.\n\n## Code example\n\n### Incorrect\n```html\n<iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/abc123\"></iframe>\n```\n\n### Correct\n```html\n<iframe\n  src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/abc123\"\n  title=\"Video: How to assemble the oak chair\"\n  loading=\"lazy\"\n  allowfullscreen></iframe>\n```\n\n### React / Next.js (JSX)\n```jsx\n<iframe\n  src={`https://www.youtube.com/embed/${videoId}`}\n  title={`Video: ${videoTitle}`}\n  loading=\"lazy\"\n  allowFullScreen\n/>\n```\n\n### Vue\n```vue\n<template>\n  <iframe\n    :src=\"`https://www.youtube.com/embed/${videoId}`\"\n    :title=\"`Video: ${videoTitle}`\"\n    loading=\"lazy\"\n    allowfullscreen\n  />\n</template>\n```\n\n## How to check your fix\n\nIn the browser's accessibility tree, check each iframe has a name. With a screen reader, move to the frame and confirm the title is announced. Then rescan with EveryVisitor."
