    "ruleId": "listitem",
    "platform": "custom",
    "slug": "listitem",
    "title": "Put list items inside a list",
    "summary": "li elements must sit directly inside a ul, ol or menu element.",
    "reviewedAt": "2026-11-16T00:00:00Z",
    "wrong": "An `<li>` that isn't inside a `<ul>` or `<ol>`, often because a component renders list items on their own, isn't announced as part of a list.",
    "affects": "Screen reader users, who lose the list structure and item count.",
    "howToFix": "Wrap the `<li>` elements in a `<ul>` or `<ol>`. If a component renders `<li>`, make sure every place that uses it puts it inside a list. If it isn't really a list, use a `<div>` instead.",
    "codeSnippet": "### Incorrect\n```html\n<div class=\"breadcrumbs\">\n  <li><a href=\"/\">Home</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"/chairs\">Chairs</a></li>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Correct\n```html\n<nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n  <ol class=\"breadcrumbs\">\n    <li><a href=\"/\">Home</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/chairs\" aria-current=\"page\">Chairs</a></li>\n  </ol>\n</nav>\n```\n\n### React / Next.js (JSX)\n```jsx\n<nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n  <ol>\n    {crumbs.map((c, i) => (\n      <li key={c.href}>\n        <Link href={c.href} aria-current={i === crumbs.length - 1 ? \"page\" : undefined}>\n          {c.label}\n        </Link>\n      </li>\n    ))}\n  </ol>\n</nav>\n```\n\n### Vue\n```vue\n<template>\n  <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n    <ol>\n      <li v-for=\"c in crumbs\" :key=\"c.href\"><RouterLink :to=\"c.href\">{{ c.label }}</RouterLink></li>\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n</template>\n```",
    "howToCheck": "Inspect each `<li>` in DevTools and confirm its parent is `<ul>` or `<ol>`. Then rescan with EveryVisitor.",
    "bodyMd": "# Put list items inside a list\n\n## What's wrong\n\nAn `<li>` that isn't inside a `<ul>` or `<ol>`, often because a component renders list items on their own, isn't announced as part of a list.\n\n## Who it affects\n\nScreen reader users, who lose the list structure and item count.\n\n## How to fix on a custom-coded site\n\nWrap the `<li>` elements in a `<ul>` or `<ol>`. If a component renders `<li>`, make sure every place that uses it puts it inside a list. If it isn't really a list, use a `<div>` instead.\n\n## Code example\n\n### Incorrect\n```html\n<div class=\"breadcrumbs\">\n  <li><a href=\"/\">Home</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"/chairs\">Chairs</a></li>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Correct\n```html\n<nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n  <ol class=\"breadcrumbs\">\n    <li><a href=\"/\">Home</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"/chairs\" aria-current=\"page\">Chairs</a></li>\n  </ol>\n</nav>\n```\n\n### React / Next.js (JSX)\n```jsx\n<nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n  <ol>\n    {crumbs.map((c, i) => (\n      <li key={c.href}>\n        <Link href={c.href} aria-current={i === crumbs.length - 1 ? \"page\" : undefined}>\n          {c.label}\n        </Link>\n      </li>\n    ))}\n  </ol>\n</nav>\n```\n\n### Vue\n```vue\n<template>\n  <nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n    <ol>\n      <li v-for=\"c in crumbs\" :key=\"c.href\"><RouterLink :to=\"c.href\">{{ c.label }}</RouterLink></li>\n    </ol>\n  </nav>\n</template>\n```\n\n## How to check your fix\n\nInspect each `<li>` in DevTools and confirm its parent is `<ul>` or `<ol>`. Then rescan with EveryVisitor."
