    "ruleId": "select-name",
    "platform": "custom",
    "slug": "select-name",
    "title": "Give dropdown menus a label",
    "summary": "Every select element needs a label so people know what they're choosing, such as size or sort order.",
    "reviewedAt": "2026-11-16T00:00:00Z",
    "wrong": "A `<select>` with no label is announced as \"combo box\" or \"pop-up button\" without saying what it controls.",
    "affects": "Screen reader users choosing a size, colour, quantity, country or sort order, and voice control users.",
    "howToFix": "Add a `<label>` linked to the `<select>` with `for` and `id`. If the design has no room for visible text, use visually hidden label text, or an `aria-label` as a last resort. The first option should not stand in for the label.",
    "codeSnippet": "### Incorrect\n```html\n<select name=\"sort\">\n  <option>Featured</option>\n  <option>Price, low to high</option>\n</select>\n```\n\n### Correct\n```html\n<label for=\"sort-by\">Sort by</label>\n<select id=\"sort-by\" name=\"sort\">\n  <option>Featured</option>\n  <option>Price, low to high</option>\n</select>\n```\n\n### React / Next.js (JSX)\n```jsx\nconst id = useId();\n\n<label htmlFor={id}>Size</label>\n<select id={id} value={size} onChange={(e) => setSize(e.target.value)}>\n  {sizes.map((s) => <option key={s} value={s}>{s}</option>)}\n</select>\n```\n\n### Vue\n```vue\n<template>\n  <label for=\"size\">Size</label>\n  <select id=\"size\" v-model=\"size\">\n    <option v-for=\"s in sizes\" :key=\"s\" :value=\"s\">{{ s }}</option>\n  </select>\n</template>\n```",
    "howToCheck": "Tab to the dropdown with a screen reader on and confirm it says the label, such as \"Sort by, Featured, pop-up button\". Then rescan with EveryVisitor.",
    "bodyMd": "# Give dropdown menus a label\n\n## What's wrong\n\nA `<select>` with no label is announced as \"combo box\" or \"pop-up button\" without saying what it controls.\n\n## Who it affects\n\nScreen reader users choosing a size, colour, quantity, country or sort order, and voice control users.\n\n## How to fix on a custom-coded site\n\nAdd a `<label>` linked to the `<select>` with `for` and `id`. If the design has no room for visible text, use visually hidden label text, or an `aria-label` as a last resort. The first option should not stand in for the label.\n\n## Code example\n\n### Incorrect\n```html\n<select name=\"sort\">\n  <option>Featured</option>\n  <option>Price, low to high</option>\n</select>\n```\n\n### Correct\n```html\n<label for=\"sort-by\">Sort by</label>\n<select id=\"sort-by\" name=\"sort\">\n  <option>Featured</option>\n  <option>Price, low to high</option>\n</select>\n```\n\n### React / Next.js (JSX)\n```jsx\nconst id = useId();\n\n<label htmlFor={id}>Size</label>\n<select id={id} value={size} onChange={(e) => setSize(e.target.value)}>\n  {sizes.map((s) => <option key={s} value={s}>{s}</option>)}\n</select>\n```\n\n### Vue\n```vue\n<template>\n  <label for=\"size\">Size</label>\n  <select id=\"size\" v-model=\"size\">\n    <option v-for=\"s in sizes\" :key=\"s\" :value=\"s\">{{ s }}</option>\n  </select>\n</template>\n```\n\n## How to check your fix\n\nTab to the dropdown with a screen reader on and confirm it says the label, such as \"Sort by, Featured, pop-up button\". Then rescan with EveryVisitor."
